# 144. Binary Tree Preorder Traversal

## APPROACH: BINARY TREE PREORDER TRAVERSAL

Idea:
Preorder Traversal follow karta hai: Root -> Left -> Right (N-L-R).
Har node par pehle uski value process karo, fir poora left subtree, fir poora right subtree.

--------------------------------------------------

APPROACH (Recursive / DFS)

1. Ek result list (`ans`) initialize karo.

2. Ek recursive helper function call karo: `helper(ans, root)`.

3. Base Case:
   Agar `root == null` hai, simply `return` kar jao (subtree end).

4. Current node ki value list me add karo:
   `ans.add(root.val)`

5. Left child ke liye recursive call karo:
   `helper(ans, root.left)`

6. Right child ke liye recursive call karo:
   `helper(ans, root.right)`

7. Final list `ans` return kar do.

--------------------------------------------------

EXAMPLE

Tree:
    1
     \
      2
     /
    3

Calls:
- Visit 1 -> ans = [1]
- Left of 1 is null -> return
- Right of 1 is 2 -> visit 2 -> ans = [1, 2]
- Left of 2 is 3 -> visit 3 -> ans = [1, 2, 3]
- Left & Right of 3 are null -> return
- Right of 2 is null -> return

Result: [1, 2, 3]

--------------------------------------------------

WHY RECURSION?

- Tree ek recursive data structure hai jisme har subtree apne aap me ek tree hota hai.
- Call stack naturally call order aur backtracking manage kar leta hai without extra manual pointers.

--------------------------------------------------

COMPLEXITY

N = Total number of nodes in tree
H = Height of binary tree

Time:
O(N) -> Har node exactly ek baar visit hoti hai.

Space:
O(H) -> Recursive call stack height par depend karta hai.
Worst case (skewed tree): O(N)
Best/Average case (balanced tree): O(log N)
*(Excluding output list)*

--------------------------------------------------

INTERVIEW POINT

Preorder means "Node Pehle" (Root -> Left -> Right).
Follow-up me interviewer iterative solution maang sakta hai.
Iterative me explicit Stack use karte hain: Root push karo, fir pop karte waqt pehle Right child push karo, fir Left child (kyunki stack LIFO hai, toh Left pehle pop hoga).

--------------------------------------------------

# CODE:

import java.util.*;

/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> preorderTraversal(TreeNode root) {
        List<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();
        helper(ans, root);
        return ans;
    }

    private void helper(List<Integer> ans, TreeNode root) {
        // Base case
        if (root == null) {
            return;
        }

        // Process Root -> Left -> Right
        ans.add(root.val);
        helper(ans, root.left);
        helper(ans, root.right);
    }
}
